{"case_id": "m50", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "anthropic__claude-sonnet-5.5@low", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5", "effort": "low", "group": "claude", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Exponential and logarithmic functions", "grade12"], "output": "**Solution**\n\nlog₂ x = 5\n\nConvert to exponential form, using log_b x = y ⟺ b^y = x:\n\nx = 2⁵\n\n**x = 32**\n\nCheck: log₂ 32 = 5 because 2⁵ = 32 ✓", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 1.632, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 632, "output_tokens": 88, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "cost_usd": 0.002144, "served_models": ["anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5"], "hosts": ["Claude Platform on AWS"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:04:35"}
{"case_id": "m52", "rep": 0, "suite": "maths", "variant": "anthropic__claude-sonnet-5.5@low", "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5", "effort": "low", "group": "claude", "status": "ok", "grade_level": 12, "tags": ["Functions and inverse functions", "grade12"], "output": "**Solution**\n\nf(x) = 3x − 6\n\nLet y = 3x − 6 and interchange x and y (the inverse swaps the variables):\n\nx = 3y − 6\n\nSolve for y:\n\n3y = x + 6\n\ny = (x + 6)/3\n\n**f⁻¹(x) = (x + 6)/3 = ⅓x + 2**", "pred": null, "grade": {"correct": 1.0}, "judge": null, "latency_s": 1.685, "calls": 1, "input_tokens": 599, "output_tokens": 116, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "cost_usd": 0.002358, "served_models": ["anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5"], "hosts": ["Claude Platform on AWS"], "finish_reasons": ["stop"], "judge_cost_usd": 0.0, "ts": "2026-10-31T18:04:35"}
